import Lab.Bondage.Basic

/-!
# Four deleted edges never increase the domination number

`Ls` lists 57 minimum dominating sets `D` of Yavari's graph, each with, for every vertex `x ∉ D`,
the indices of the edges joining `x` to `D` (Yavari's "bundles", Lemma 2.2). Deleting an edge set
`F` keeps `D` dominating as long as `F` contains no whole bundle. `checkQ` verifies, for every
multiset `a ≤ b ≤ c ≤ d` of four edge indices, that some listed `D` survives. The list was chosen
greedily by `explorer/bondage/gen_quads.py`; `validL` re-checks every entry against the graph.
-/

namespace OpenProblemsLab.Bondage

